>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>To make the most of the smartphone, it is important to &lt;b&gt;familiarise yourself with&lt;/b&gt; all of its many features. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>He found it difficult to [adapt himself to] working in the banking sector in London, and moved back to Italy after only a year. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6013.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>He found it difficult to &lt;b&gt;adapt himself to&lt;/b&gt; working in the banking sector in London, and moved back to Italy after only a year. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>He was late, so he hurried to the bathroom, [washed himself] quickly, and dashed downstairs. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6014.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>He was late, so he hurried to the bathroom, &lt;b&gt;washed himself&lt;/b&gt; quickly, and dashed downstairs. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Guests and visitors alike can [avail themselves of] the excellent facilities that the hotel offers. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6015.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Guests and visitors alike can &lt;b&gt;avail themselves of&lt;/b&gt; the excellent facilities that the hotel offers. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>A recent issue of &lt;i&gt;Science in the World&lt;/i&gt; [concerned itself with] developments in tidal power. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6016.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>A recent issue of &lt;i&gt;Science in the World&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;concerned itself with&lt;/b&gt; developments in tidal power. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Try to understand the general points, but don't [trouble yourself with|trouble yourself with|concern yourself with] the details for the moment. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6017.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Try to understand the general points, but don't &lt;b&gt;trouble yourself with&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;concern yourself with&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;trouble yourself about&lt;/b&gt; the details for the moment. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>When their mother called them in for dinner, Maya and Maxine [hid themselves] behind some bushes at the bottom of the garden. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6018.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>When their mother called them in for dinner, Maya and Maxine &lt;b&gt;hid themselves&lt;/b&gt; behind some bushes at the bottom of the garden. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>While we were waiting for the taxi to arrive, we [busied ourselves|busied ourselves with|occupied ourselves with] checking that we had tickets and passports. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/6019.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>While we were waiting for the taxi to arrive, we &lt;b&gt;busied ourselves&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;busied ourselves with&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;occupied ourselves with&lt;/b&gt; checking that we had tickets and passports. </modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Martha [prides herself on|prided herself on] her cooking, and was quite upset when Paul said he didn't want anything to eat. </text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/60110.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Martha &lt;b&gt;prides herself on&lt;/b&gt; / &lt;b&gt;prided herself on&lt;/b&gt; her cooking, and was quite upset when Paul said he didn't want anything to eat. </modelAnswerString></question></question_xml><enableAudioOnChecked>false</enableAudioOnChecked><enableAudioOnClosed>true</enableAudioOnClosed><correctFeedback_str /><incorrectFeedback_str /><attemptsAllowed>1</attemptsAllowed></mcq_xml></params_xml><alignment>left</alignment><alignPercent>95</alignPercent><custom_style_name /><sharedTokenBankId /><is_sequential>False</is_sequential><is_compulsory>False</is_compulsory><states><state id="queued" visible="True" enabled="False" /><state id="in_progress" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="complete" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="checked" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="closed" visible="True" enabled